# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
artifacts/

# Local test data captured from the reference server
traces/
*.trace
*.gg2trace

# ...except the recordings the tests are built on. Those are oracles, not
# scratch data: WeaponBlockTests and PhysicsParityTests assert they exist, so
# without this a fresh clone fails two tests that pass on the machine that
# recorded them. docs/PARITY.md says parity fixtures live with the tests and
# run in CI; this is what makes that true.
!tests/GG2.Tests/Fixtures/*.trace
!tests/GG2.Tests/Fixtures/duel/*.trace

# Agent workflow (CLAUDE.md, .claude/) is local to each checkout and kept in a
# separate private repository.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/

# The bot nav graphs at nav/ are checked in deliberately: without them a clone
# cannot run a bot. Hex text compresses about 28:1, so they cost ~1.2 MB packed.
TestResults/

# Fleet analytics collected by scripts/fleet-analytics.sh. Player names; never commit.
deploy/analytics/

# scripts/ is the operator's own fleet tooling (deploy, build wrappers, tunnels),
# specific to the hosts the author runs. docs/DEPLOY.md, CONFIG.md, WEBADMIN.md
# and ANALYTICS.md describe the layout it implements.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `scripts/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, so a future src/Something/scripts/ would be ignored
# silently and nothing would go red.
/scripts/

# The web panel's own identity (Certificate=auto, FleetMember=1) when run with no --config.
web-cert.pfx
fleet-member.token
